Z||000008||mshill||10-16-2000||03:15 PM||||Lat month I ordered from carparts.com and had a coupon for $50 off a purchase of $100 or more.  I ordered a bunch of stuff (filters, gaskets, sensors, etc).  The stuff started coming in about a week, but it can in like five different shipments.<P>I have used wrenchhead as well.  They are faster and only one in maybe five times did they have to ship a single order in more than one shipment.  I take that to mean they have more of the stuff in stock instead of playing the "just in time" stocking philosophy.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||PatrickB||10-16-2000||04:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>I have used wrenchhead as well.  They are faster and only one in maybe five times did they have to ship a single order in more than one shipment.  I take that to mean they have more of the stuff in stock instead of playing the "just in time" stocking philosophy.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well the whole thing with carparts is that it is not one company.  They use the North American Parts Network which is a ton of wholesalers all over the country.  Depending on what you order is going to be where it comes from.  IE: One company might carry only gaskets, one company will carry alternators. So your whole order will rarely ever come together.<BR>This also means that carparts doesnt have as much control over your order as you think. Like what happened with my order.  The wholesaler was not shipping my order and being a pain and carparts was pretty much helpless.  All they kept doing was calling them but nothing was getting done.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Black88GT||10-16-2000||07:01 PM||||I've had the same experience as mshill.  It might take longer then other places but you can't beat the prices.  If I need something in a hurry I will order elsewhere...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
